[{"url": "https://www.biarrinetworks.com/blog/automated-permitting-workflow", "title": "Automated permitting workflow | Biarri Networks", "content": "Biarri Networks\n\nAutomated permitting workflow\n\nAutomated permitting workflow\n\nOne of the most time-consuming parts of OSP fiber construction is managing the permitting process. Even with well-designed plans, most projects encounter permitting kickbacks\u2014errors, missing data, or format issues that require revisions and resubmissions.\n\nBiarri ICP now includes a permitting workflow module that helps manage, track, and automate parts of this process. Here\u2019s how it works:\n\n1. Track permit applications across jurisdictions\n\nICP allows project managers to create and manage permit applications by jurisdiction, status, and type. This includes managing contacts, submission dates, expiry dates, and notes.\n\n2. Link permits to design segments and tasks\n\nEach permit application can be linked to specific design segments in the project. This means that when a permit is approved (or rejected), the project manager can immediately see which construction tasks are affected.\n\nICP also tracks permit rejection rates\u2014so if certain permit types or jurisdictions are consistently rejecting applications, this data is visible in the dashboard.\n\n3. Automate document generation for permit submissions\n\nICP can generate documents required for permit submissions, using templates that can be customized to specific jurisdictions. This reduces the manual effort required to prepare permit packages.\n\nICP can generate documents required for permit submissions, using templates that can be automate to specific jurisdictions.\n\nICP can generate documents required for permit submissions, using templates that can be customized to specific jurisdictions. This reduces the manual effort required to prepare permit packages.\n\n4. Track permit status and approvals\n\nAll permit applications are tracked in a central dashboard, wi